---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/legal-layout.astro";
import { LINKS } from "@/constants/links";
import { ROUTES } from "@/constants/routes";
import { SPONSOR_PORTAL_URL } from "@/constants/sponsors";
---

<LegalLayout
  id="refunds"
  heading="Refund policy"
  title="Refund Policy"
  description="Cancellation and refund policy for Shadcn Labs sponsorships paid through GitHub Sponsors or Dodo Payments."
  updated="Nov 01, 2026"
>
  <p>
    Sponsorships are monthly subscriptions. Most sponsors pay through{" "}
    <a
      class="link-underline"
      href="https://github.com/sponsors/shadcn-labs"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener">GitHub Sponsors</a
    >; teams that cannot use GitHub pay through Dodo Payments, our merchant of
    record. Refunds are issued by the provider that took your payment, to your
    original payment method.
  </p>

  <h3>Cancelling</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>GitHub Sponsors:</strong> change your amount or cancel at any time
      from your GitHub account under your sponsorships. GitHub confirms the
      change to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Dodo Payments:</strong> cancel from the <a
        class="link-underline"
        href={SPONSOR_PORTAL_URL}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Dodo customer portal</a
      >, or email <a class="link-underline" href={`mailto:${LINKS.EMAIL}`}>{LINKS.EMAIL}</a
      >.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Cancellation stops future renewals; your placements stay live until the end
    of the period you already paid for.
  </p>

  <h3>GitHub Sponsors payments</h3>
  <p>
    GitHub decides whether a GitHub payment is refundable, under{" "}
    <a
      class="link-underline"
      href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/github-terms/github-sponsors-additional-terms"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener">GitHub's sponsor terms</a
    >. If you were charged in error, or we cannot deliver the perks of your
    tier, email us and we will work with GitHub to sort it out. Cancelling stops
    future charges either way.
  </p>

  <h3>Dodo Payments refunds</h3>
  <p>We issue a full refund through Dodo Payments when:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You ask within 7 days of your first payment and your placements have not
      gone live yet.
    </li>
    <li>You were charged more than once for the same period.</li>
    <li>
      We cannot deliver the perks of your tier, or we remove your sponsorship
      under our <a class="link-underline" href={ROUTES.TERMS}>terms</a> (in that
      case, for the unused part of the period).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>When we do not refund</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Partial months after your placements have gone live. Cancel before the
      next renewal instead.
    </li>
    <li>Renewals you did not cancel before the renewal date.</li>
    <li>Results such as traffic, clicks, or conversions being lower than hoped.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>How to ask</h3>
  <p>
    Email <a class="link-underline" href={`mailto:${LINKS.EMAIL}`}>{LINKS.EMAIL}</a> with the email you
    paid with, the provider (GitHub or Dodo), and your invoice, receipt, or
    subscription ID. We reply within 3 business days, and approved refunds
    usually reach you within 5–10 business days, depending on your bank. Please
    contact us before opening a chargeback; we resolve most issues faster that
    way.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
